From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:13:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Disable PCIe port 0 for now

The device tree on this branch enables three blocks for the first time
on the 14-inch MacBook Pro (M4, 2024): PCIe port 0 (the BCM4388
Wi-Fi/Bluetooth module) with its DART, the two USB-C ports with their
SPMI port controllers, and the AOP audio group. With it the machine
hangs early in boot: the boot logo stays up and nothing is printed,
both with this kernel and with an older one (MEASURED 2026-11-04). The
same device tree with these three blocks disabled, and nothing else
changed, boots with this kernel (MEASURED 2026-11-04).

Which of the three blocks causes the hang, alone or only in
combination, is not known yet (root cause TO-VERIFY). Disable PCIe
port 0 and its DART until a J604 boot with them enabled has been shown
to work. Only the status lines change, so enabling them again is a
revert of this change.

While pcie0 and its port are disabled, m1n1 does not act on them: it
writes the radio's power rail and puts the radio's DART stream into
bypass only for an enabled host and port.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 008c746010..ccb3210c3b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -202,21 +202,25 @@
  * "guam"). m1n1 powers it through the same SMC action as pwren-gpios and
  * fills in the addresses, antenna SKU and calibration below. Port 1 is not
  * wired; port 2 (the SD card reader) stays off.
+ *
+ * Disabled for now: a J604 device tree that enables this port together with
+ * the USB-C ports and the AOP hangs early boot, before the console. Enable
+ * it again once a J604 boot with it enabled has been shown to work.
  */
 
 &pcie0_dart {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-PCIE-3..5 */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-PCIE-3..5 */
 };
 
 &pcie0 {
 	iommu-map = <0x100 &pcie0_dart 1 1>;
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-PCIE-1, DTV-PCIE-2 */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-PCIE-1, DTV-PCIE-2 */
 };
 
 &pcie0_port0 {
 	pwren-gpios = <&smc_gpio 0x13 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* DTV-PCIE-11 */
 	bus-range = <1 1>;
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-PCIE-6, DTV-PCIE-7 */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-PCIE-6, DTV-PCIE-7 */
 
 	wifi0: wifi@0,0 {
 		compatible = "pci14e4,4434"; /* DTV-WLAN-1 */
